# CRIMEGRAPH AI - General Rules

1. Always follow the vertical slice development workflow:
   - Understand -> Plan -> Implement -> Test -> Review -> Commit -> Update Docs.
2. Read `docs/PRD.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/RULES.md` before making architectural changes.
3. Every graph entity or edge must include an evidence provenance link (document ID, offset, or transaction reference).
4. Never leave unused imports, dead code, or temporary console logs.
5. All commits must follow conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `sec:`, `test:`, `docs:`.
